{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (via the cobbler orchestrator) is requesting implementation of task #5302: \"[stitch] cmd/md5sum -- srd030 R2.1-R2.4\". This is a code generation task to implement checksum verification mode (--check/-c) for the md5sum utility, including:\n   - R2.1: --check FILE reads and verifies checksums in GNU/BSD format\n   - R2.2: Print \"FILENAME: OK\" or \"FILENAME: FAILED\", exit 1 on failures\n   - R2.3: --warn (-w) prints warnings for malformed lines\n   - R2.4: --quiet suppresses OK lines; --status suppresses all output\n   \n   Files to modify: `cmd/md5sum/main.go` and `cmd/md5sum/md5sum_test.go`.\n   Design decisions mandate using `pkg/hashutil.VerifyChecksums` and `pkg/hashutil.CheckOptions`.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - GNU md5sum checksum verification protocol (--check mode)\n   - Differential testing against `gmd5sum` Homebrew reference binary\n   - pkg/hashutil contract: `VerifyChecksums(checksumFile string, cfg HashConfig, opts CheckOptions, stdout, stderr io.Writer) (bool, error)`\n   - pkg/hashutil contract: `CheckOptions struct { Warn bool; Quiet bool; Status bool }`\n   - pkg/hashutil contract: `ParseChecksumLine` for GNU/BSD format parsing\n   - SIGPIPE handling via `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - pkg/testutils `DiffTest` struct and `RunDiffTests` for differential testing\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd030-md5sum.yaml** (read, lines 1-127)\n     - Contains R2.1-R2.4 requirements for check mode\n     - Non-goals: no --strict flag, no HMAC-MD5\n     - R2.1: Parse GNU format (HASH  FILENAME or HASH *FILENAME) and BSD tag format\n     - R2.2: Print OK/FAILED, exit 1 on any failure\n     - R2.3: --warn for malformed lines, silent skip without it\n     - R2.4: --quiet suppresses OK, --status suppresses all output\n\n   - **cmd/md5sum/main.go** (read, 118 lines, existing implementation)\n     - Already contains check mode implementation using `hashutil.VerifyChecksums`\n     - Already has `options` struct with `check`, `warn`, `quiet`, `status` fields\n     - Already parses --check, --warn, --quiet, --status long flags and -c, -w short flags\n     - Check mode logic at lines 24-41: iterates files, calls VerifyChecksums, sets exitCode\n     - May need minor adjustments but core R2 functionality appears present\n     ```go\n     if opts.check {\n         checkOpts := hashutil.CheckOptions{\n             Warn:   opts.warn,\n             Quiet:  opts.quiet,\n             Status: opts.status,\n         }\n         exitCode := 0\n         for _, f := range files {\n             ok, err := hashutil.VerifyChecksums(f, cfg, checkOpts, os.Stdout, os.Stderr)\n             if err != nil {\n                 fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"md5sum: %s\\n\", err)\n                 exitCode = 1\n             } else if !ok {\n                 exitCode = 1\n             }\n         }\n         os.Exit(exitCode)\n     }\n     ```\n\n   - **cmd/md5sum/md5sum_test.go** (read, 108 lines, existing tests)\n     - Contains only R1.x tests (digest computation): stdin, single file, binary mode, tag format, multiple files, missing file\n     - NO R2.x test cases exist - this is the primary gap to fill\n     - Uses `testutils.BuildBinary`, `exec.LookPath(\"gmd5sum\")`, creates temp files\n     - Pattern: create fixture files, define `[]testutils.DiffTest` slice, call `testutils.RunDiffTests`\n     ```go\n     func TestDiff(t *testing.T) {\n         goBin := testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")\n         refBin, err := exec.LookPath(\"gmd5sum\")\n         if err != nil { t.Skip(\"reference binary not found\") }\n         // ... creates helloFile, emptyFile in tmpDir\n         tests := []testutils.DiffTest{ /* R1.x tests only */ }\n