to verify no issues (AC5)\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading all three required files (SRD, main.go, test file) and the hashutil package contract. I was about to plan the implementation approach. The main.go appears to already have R2.1-R2.4 functionality wired up. The primary work remaining is:\n   1. Verify main.go is complete for R2 (it looks like it is)\n   2. Add R2.x differential test cases to md5sum_test.go (the main gap)\n   3. The test cases need to: create checksum files using the known MD5 of fixture files, then run md5sum --check against them with various flag combinations (--warn, --quiet, --status)\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Write the implementation - primarily adding R2.1-R2.4 test cases to `cmd/md5sum/md5sum_test.go`. The test setup needs to:\n   1. Generate a valid checksum file by writing the known MD5 hash of `helloFile` in GNU format\n   2. Generate an invalid checksum file with a wrong hash\n   3. Generate a checksum file with malformed lines\n   4. Add DiffTest entries for: `--check` valid, `--check` with mismatch (exit 1), `--check --warn` with malformed lines, `--check --quiet`, `--check --status`\n   \n   Also need to verify if main.go needs any changes - it looks complete but should confirm the `gmd5sum` warning message format matches (the `md5sum:` prefix in error messages at line 35).\n\n   The task description says: \"requirements: R1: Implement srd030-md5sum R2.1 per the SRD specification, R2: Implement srd030-md5sum R2.2, R3: Implement srd030-md5sum R2.3, R4: Implement srd030-md5sum R2.4\" and \"acceptance_criteria: AC1: All R2.1-R2.4 requirements from srd030-md5sum are implemented, AC2: Differential tests for R2.1-R2.4 pass against gmd5sum reference binary, AC3: go build succeeds, AC4: go test passes, AC5: go vet reports no issues\"\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/