{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01651MjpUcusLWLUGbUNLcdE","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n2\t// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n3\t\n4\t// Package hashutil provides shared hash output formatting and checksum\n5\t// verification logic for md5sum, sha1sum, sha256sum, sha512sum, sha224sum,\n6\t// sha384sum, b2sum, cksum, and sum utilities.\n7\t// Implements srd086-hashutil R1.1, R1.2, R1.3, R1.4.\n8\tpackage hashutil\n9\t\n10\timport (\n11\t\t\"encoding/hex\"\n12\t\t\"fmt\"\n13\t\t\"hash\"\n14\t\t\"io\"\n15\t)\n16\t\n17\t// HashConfig parameterizes a hash utility with its algorithm name, hash\n18\t// factory, and expected digest length. (R1.1)\n19\ttype HashConfig struct {\n20\t\tAlgorithm string\n21\t\tNewHash   func() hash.Hash\n22\t\tDigestLen int\n23\t}\n24\t\n25\t// CheckOptions controls --check mode output behavior. (R1.2 / R2.2)\n26\ttype CheckOptions struct {\n27\t\tWarn   bool\n28\t\tQuiet  bool\n29\t\tStatus bool\n30\t}\n31\t\n32\t// FormatGNU formats a digest and filename in GNU coreutils format.\n33\t// Text mode: \"HASH  FILENAME\"; binary mode: \"HASH *FILENAME\". (R1.3)\n34\tfunc FormatGNU(digest, filename string, binary bool) string {\n35\t\tif binary {\n36\t\t\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"%s *%s\", digest, filename)\n37\t\t}\n38\t\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"%s  %s\", digest, filename)\n39\t}\n40\t\n41\t// FormatBSDTag formats a digest in BSD tag format:\n42\t// \"ALGORITHM (FILENAME) = HASH\". (R1.3)\n43\tfunc FormatBSDTag(algorithm, filename, digest string) string {\n44\t\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"%s (%s) = %s\", algorithm, filename, digest)\n45\t}\n46\t\n47\t// ComputeDigest reads all bytes from r, computes the hash using cfg, and\n48\t// returns the lowercase hex-encoded digest string. (R1.4)\n49\tfunc ComputeDigest(r io.Reader, cfg HashConfig) (string, error) {\n50\t\th := cfg.NewHash()\n51\t\tif _, err := io.Copy(h, r); err != nil {\n52\t\t\treturn \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"computing digest: %w\", err)\n53\t\t}\n54\t\treturn hex.EncodeToString(h.Sum(nil)), nil\n55\t}\n56\t\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01GJqRR8pEyk1m7SU5jiizVg","session_id":"e1c05299-c59e-492b-8da4-c8bf36b8243e","uuid":"7ee0a581-8960-4670-99e5-70efce9680ea","timestamp":"2026-05-19T22:12:50.554Z"}
