{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GJqRR8pEyk1m7SU5jiizVg","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I've read all the Go files in the pkg/hashutil package. Here's the complete analysis you requested:\n\n## pkg/hashutil Package Analysis\n\n### 1. VerifyChecksums Function Signature and Behavior\n\n**Location:** hashutil.go, lines 30-39\n\n**Signature:**\n```go\nfunc VerifyChecksums(checksumFile string, cfg HashConfig, opts CheckOptions, stdout, stderr io.Writer) (bool, error)\n```\n\n**Behavior:**\n- Reads a checksum file and verifies each entry against actual file digests\n- Returns a boolean indicating if all checks passed and an error if file operations fail\n- Takes a CheckOptions struct to control output behavior\n- Writes results to stdout and stderr according to the options\n- Implements requirement R2.3\n\n### 2. CheckOptions Struct\n\n**Location:** hashconfig.go, lines 26-30\n\n```go\ntype CheckOptions struct {\n\tWarn   bool\n\tQuiet  bool\n\tStatus bool\n}\n```\n\n**Controls:**\n- `Warn`: When true (and Status is false), prints \"WARNING: improperly formatted checksum line\" to stderr for malformed entries\n- `Quiet`: When true (and Status is false), suppresses OK messages\n- `Status`: When true, suppresses all output (both failures and successes)\n\n### 3. ParseChecksumLine Function - Supported Formats\n\n**Location:** hashutil.go, lines 19-28\n\n**Signature:**\n```go\nfunc ParseChecksumLine(line string, cfg HashConfig) (filename, expectedDigest string, binary bool, err error)\n```\n\n**Supports two formats:**\n\n1. **BSD Tag Format:** `ALGORITHM (FILENAME) = HASH`\n   - Regex: `^(\\S+) \\((.+)\\) = ([0-9a-fA-F]+)$`\n   - Example: `SHA256 (myfile.txt) = abc123def456...`\n   - Returns: binary=false\n\n2. **GNU Format:** `HASH <space_indicator>FILENAME`\n   - Regex: `^([0-9a-fA-F]+) ([ *])(.+)$`\n   - Text mode: `HASH  FILENAME` (two spaces, space indicator ' ')\n   - Binary mode: `HASH *FILENAME` (asterisk indicator '*')\n   - Returns: binary=true if space indicator is '*', false if ' '\n\nReturns error \"malformed checksum line\" if neither format matches.\n\n### 4. FormatGNU Function\n\n**Location:** hashconfig.go, lines 32-39\n\n```go\nfunc FormatGNU(digest, filename string, binary bool) string {\n\tif binary {\n\t\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"%s *%s\", digest, filename)\n\t}\n\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"%s  %s\", digest, filename)\n}\n```\n\n**Output format:**\n- **Text mode** (binary=false): `HASH  FILENAME` (digest, two spaces, filename)\n- **Binary mode** (binary=true): `HASH *FILENAME` (digest, space, asterisk, filename)\n\n### 5. Error and Warning Message Format\n\n**Stderr messages (from verifyOneLine, lines 55-80):**\n\n1. **Malformed checksum line warning:**\n   - Condition: Parse error, Warn=true, Status=false\n   - Message: `\"WARNING: improperly formatted checksum line\\n\"`\n   - Location: hashutil.go, line 59\n\n2. **File open/read failure:**\n   - Condition: computeFileDigest returns error, Status=false\n   - Message: `\"%s: FAILED open or read\\n\"` (filename + \": FAILED open or read\")\n   - Location: hashutil.go, line 66\n\n3. **Digest mismatch:**\n   - Condition: actual != expected, Status=false\n   - Message: `\"%s: FAILED\\n\"` (filename + \": FAILED\")\n   - Location: hashutil.go, line 72\n\n4. **Success message (to stdout when Status=false, Quiet=false):**\n   - Message: `\"%s: OK\\n\"` (filename + \": OK\")\n   - Location: hashutil.go, line 77\n\nAll messages use `fmt.Fprintf` for precise control over output writer selection."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e1c05299-c59e-492b-8da4-c8bf36b8243e","uuid":"52be39f7-bc30-4106-aa64-42c9270daad4","timestamp":"2026-05-19T22:12:59.652Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"In the repo at /private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5302, find and read the pkg/hashutil package. I need to understand:\n1. The VerifyChecksums function signat